
2026-03-25  pmcnary / NMICA  <pmcnary@nmica.net>

	* Phase 1 SVR5 / 32-bit portability audit — all five fixes confirmed correct.
	  See individual P1-N markers in source for detail.

	* isaudit.c (ivbauditrecord): P1-6 — lazy-initialise tvbpid / tvbuid when
	  logging has never been started (islogopen not called).  vb_rtd->tvbpid is
	  0 after calloc; PID 0 is never a valid user process on UNIX, so it is a
	  safe sentinel.  Without this fix, every audit record written in a process
	  that only uses audit (no transaction log) shows au_procid=0 / au_userid=0.
	  Fix: call getpid()/getuid() once on first entry to ivbauditrecord when
	  tvbpid is still 0.  Subsequent calls skip the check.  Both Linux and
	  SCO SVR5 guarantee PID > 0 for all user processes.

